  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Arid soil is found in dry and desert regions where rainfall is very low
    and evaporation is high. It is usually sandy, light in texture, and contains
    very little moisture and humus.


    Because of the dry climate, only sparse
    vegetation such as cactus, thorny bushes, and drought-resistant plants can grow
    naturally. High evaporation may also cause salts to accumulate near the soil
    surface.


    Main Features


    Dry and sandy texture

    Very low moisture

    Low
    humus and organic matter

    Salt deposits may be present

    Sparse vegetation

    Common
    in desert and semi-arid regions


    Improving Arid Soil


    With proper irrigation
    and the addition of organic matter, arid soil can become more suitable for growing
    crops.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
